60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, Option A is a trap. The neighbouring block’s arrears prove it fractures us. We need a system that doesn’t require constant enforcement or billing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! But the riders said they’d rather pay than be equal. Option A might work if we keep it simple. What about the lottery?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, the riders' preference for payment ignores the physical reality. Option C’s double-tier racks solve the rain and congestion, but the hoisting effort is a daily burden.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, the riders want to pay, but the ledger is empty. Option A means a levy for capital work. I need to know if the income covers the hassle.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, Option A adds billing to the existing three hours. That is a quiet collapse. Option C requires no accounting, only physical effort.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, the riders' preference is irrelevant if the system collapses. Option A creates arrears and absenteeism, exactly what we must avoid. We need zero administrative burden.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I hear you! But the riders really want to pay. Option A feels fair, even if it’s a bit of work. I’m leaning that way!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, riders wanting to pay doesn't fix the wet saddles. Option C solves the rain and congestion, but the hoisting is a daily physical burden.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, ""fair"" is a luxury. The ledger is empty, so Option A means a levy. I’m checking if the income covers the headache.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the riders' preference is a trap. Option A adds billing to the existing three hours. That is a quiet collapse. Option C requires no accounting, only physical effort.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the hoisting burden is real, but Option C eliminates the social friction and administrative collapse. It is the only choice that preserves our community without creating new enemies.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I get the worry! But the riders really want to pay. Option A feels fair, even if it’s a bit of work. I’m leaning that way!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, social friction is a symptom, not the disease. The rain and the shoving match are the disease. Option C treats the physical reality, even if the hoisting is annoying.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the hoisting is a nuisance, not a crisis. Option A generates 2,600 yen monthly. That covers the greasing and the headache. I’m voting A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the income covers the greasing, but not the collapse. Three hours becomes five. Option C requires no accounting, only physical effort. I am voting C.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, money doesn't buy community. Option A creates debtors and enemies. Option C is the only path that avoids the administrative collapse and social fracture we just documented. I am voting C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I hear your worry! But the riders really want to pay. Option A feels fair, even if it’s a bit of work. I’m leaning that way!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, preference for payment doesn't fix wet saddles or blocked exits. Option C addresses the physical reality. I am voting C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, ""fair"" is a luxury. The ledger is empty, so Option A means a levy. I’m checking if the income covers the headache.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the riders' preference is a trap. Option A adds billing to the existing three hours. That is a quiet collapse. Option C requires no accounting, only physical effort. I am voting C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
